articles.content_en:
Foreign vessels, their crew members and passengers, when entering the ports on boundary rivers and the connecting rivers with neighboring countries, are prohibited from the following acts:
(1) Photography and drawing;
(2) Swimming, fishing and hunting;
(3) Sounding;
(4) Dumping or discharging ballast, cinders, garbage, waste oil, oily water, etc. in the port.

Where a foreign vessel is in any of the following circumstances, the Harbour Superintendency may prohibit it from departing:
(1) It is not in a seaworthy condition;
(2) It violates the provisions on safe navigation;
(3) It has not paid port charges;
(4) It has not paid the compensation payable or provided appropriate security.
